error[Z0401]: `group:` belongs to the one-way form of `anova`; with a formula the groups are its terms
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:27
  |
2 | d.anova(y ~ a * b, group: a)
  |                           ^ not used with a formula
  |
  = help: write the grouping variable as a term, `anova(y ~ g)`; or name the variable alone, `anova(y, group: g)`, for the one-way test

