error[Z0401]: `equal_var:` belongs to the one-way form of `anova`; the table of a formula always pools the variance
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:31
  |
2 | d.anova(y ~ a * b, equal_var: true)
  |                               ^^^^ not used with a formula
  |
  = help: leave `equal_var:` out; Welch's F, which does not pool, is `anova(y, group: g)`

