error[Z0401]: `type:` belongs to the factorial form of `anova`, which takes a formula
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:28
  |
2 | d.anova(y, group: a, type: 3)
  |                            ^ not used with a variable and `group:`
  |
  = help: write the model as a formula, `anova(y ~ a * b, type: 3)`; the one-way test of a variable has one term and no type of sums of squares

note: `a` replaced the variable of that name (line 1)
note: `b` replaced the variable of that name (line 1)
error[Z0401]: `type:` of `anova` must be 1, 2 or 3, not 4
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:26
  |
2 | d.anova(y ~ a * b, type: 4)
  |                          ^ not a type of sums of squares
  |
  = help: `type: 1` adjusts each term for the terms above it, `type: 2` (the default) for every other term that does not contain it, `type: 3` for every other term

error[Z0401]: `type` of `anova` must be an Int, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:26
  |
2 | d.anova(y ~ a * b, type: "2")
  |                          ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: usage: `data.anova(var, group: Var, equal_var: Bool = false, weights: Var, weight_type: frequency | analytic | sampling = sampling, type: Int = 2, effect: eta | omega | omega_f | epsilon = eta)`

